    "NeurIPS 2024 main Theorems 2.1 and 2.2 specifications, reviewed by Shuangping Li on 25 September 2026",
    "indexed infinite-language oracle families, exact presentations with repetitions, finite observed prefixes, and input-relative freshness",
    "Theorem 2.1 finite-query output interface, with a target- and presentation-dependent stabilization time and no target-index input to the generator",
    "Theorem 2.2 fixed-sample interface: a family-wide distinct-sample threshold, infinite pairwise-distinct target outputs outside the supplied sample, and proof-irrelevant enumeration",
    "the explicit universe-coding interfaces theorem_2_1_of_equiv and theorem_2_2_of_equiv, including encoded oracle queries and decoded outputs",
    "recursive statement-relevant definition bodies and structure fields; supporting proof-certificate types are tracked only to guard those definitions, not as separate human audits of their claims"
  ],
  "not_automatically_tracked": [
    "theorem proof bodies and intermediate mathematical proof-step correspondence",
    "algorithm and construction correspondence, including finite-query termination, criticality, and stabilization arguments",
    "supporting-lemma and generated proof-certificate proof correspondence",
    "the separate Section 4 semantic Level 3 construction and observed-set implementation",
    "classically selected countable-universe wrappers and computability of the supplied oracle or universe coding",
    "runtime and numerical membership-query complexity",
    "robust-prompt Result 7.1 and the informal pairwise-distinct-output modification of countable-family Result 2.1"
